From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The SCSP thread sleeps to its deadline instead of polling

ScspAsynMainRealtime, the sound CPU's thread in the realtime mode the
retro_arena port uses, waits for the next block of samples with
pthread_cond_timedwait. Its Linux branch put time() into a timespec and passed
ctime() of it, a string, as the deadline: the call failed with EINVAL at once,
so the thread looped calling ctime(), which stats /etc/localtime each time,
until the block was due. The deadline is now clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME)
plus the sleep, normalised.

On an RG52 Mini, Resident Evil, 90 s, with patch 13: the thread 98% of a core
before, 17% after; the process 186-195% against 105%, all four cores 49-51%
busy against 28%; the same 59.9 fps; 73-75 C at the end against 78.

